@* =============================================================================
   SECTION 21: _ViewImports — TAG HELPER REGISTRATION & GLOBAL USINGS
   =============================================================================
   FILE ROLE: Applies @using directives and @addTagHelper registrations to every
              Razor view in Views/ and all sub-folders.  Loaded once at startup;
              settings cascade down the folder hierarchy.
   =============================================================================

   @using DIRECTIVES:
     With ImplicitUsings disabled, Razor views see ONLY the namespaces listed here.
     Add a namespace here to avoid fully-qualified type names in @model declarations
     and inline Razor expressions.

     RoutingAttributeRouting       — top-level types (none needed here, included for completeness)
     RoutingAttributeRouting.Models — makes RouteDebugViewModel available without full qualification

   HOW _ViewImports SCOPING WORKS:
     The Razor engine walks UP the directory tree from each view file, collecting every
     _ViewImports.cshtml it finds and applying them outer-to-inner.  A file in
     Views/Home/_ViewImports.cshtml would EXTEND this root-level file, not replace it.

   @addTagHelper SYNTAX:
     @addTagHelper  TypePattern,  AssemblyName
       TypePattern   — "*" for all types, or a fully-qualified class name to include one
       AssemblyName  — the assembly/dll name (matches the .csproj name, NOT the namespace)

   LINE 1 — built-in ASP.NET Core tag helpers:
     Assembly: Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
     Includes:
       AnchorTagHelper    — <a asp-action asp-controller asp-route-* asp-route asp-area>
       FormTagHelper      — <form asp-action asp-controller asp-antiforgery>
       InputTagHelper     — <input asp-for />
       LabelTagHelper     — <label asp-for></label>
       SelectTagHelper    — <select asp-for asp-items>
       TextAreaTagHelper  — <textarea asp-for></textarea>
       ValidationTagHelper — <span asp-validation-for>
       EnvironmentTagHelper — <environment include="Development">
       PartialTagHelper   — <partial name="_PartialView" />
       CacheTagHelper     — <cache expires-after="...">
       ImageTagHelper     — <img asp-append-version="true">
       LinkTagHelper      — <link asp-append-version="true">
       ScriptTagHelper    — <script asp-append-version="true">

   LINE 2 — custom tag helpers from this project's assembly:
     Assembly: RoutingAttributeRouting (from RoutingAttributeRouting.csproj)
     This project defines no custom tag helpers; the line is included to show
     the correct syntax and is harmless when no custom helpers exist.

   @removeTagHelper — OPT OUT:
     @removeTagHelper Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers.FormTagHelper,
         Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
     Use when a built-in helper conflicts with existing HTML or a third-party helper.

   @tagHelperPrefix — REQUIRE A PREFIX:
     @tagHelperPrefix th:
     After this, only <th:form asp-action="..."> activates the tag helper;
     plain <form asp-action="..."> is treated as regular HTML.
     Useful in content-heavy pages mixing tag helper markup with raw HTML.
*@
@using RoutingAttributeRouting
@using RoutingAttributeRouting.Models
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, RoutingAttributeRouting
